lar al del ave lira, debido a que toma sonidos que escucha para componerlo. Es también conocido como <b>“cenzontle” de agua</b>, <b>mirlo pardo</b> o <b>mirlo huertero</b>.\", \"observations_count\": 22868, \"conservation_status\": null, \"english_common_name\": \"Clay-colored Thrush\", \"taxon_changes_count\": 0, \"taxon_schemes_count\": 9, \"conservation_statuses\": [{\"id\": 4999, \"url\": \"https://www.iucnredlist.org/species/22708914/132078490\", \"iucn\": 10, \"place\": null, \"status\": \"LC\", \"taxon_id\": 12720, \"authority\": \"IUCN Red List\", \"source_id\": 18766, \"created_at\": \"2013-02-16T00:52:34+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": \"open\", \"taxon_name\": \"Turdus grayi\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2020-01-19T12:40:50+00:00\", \"updater_id\": null, \"description\": null}], \"preferred_common_name\": \"Mirlo Café\", \"complete_species_count\": null, \"current_synonymous_taxon_ids\": null}], \"per_page\": 30, \"total_results\": 1}', NULL, '2025-12-15 05:41:49', '2025-12-14 05:41:49', 0, '2025-12-14 05:41:49', '2025-12-14 05:41:49'),
