n\": \"(c) cello caruso-turiello, some rights reserved (CC BY), uploaded by cello caruso-turiello\", \"license_code\": \"cc-by\", \"attribution_name\": \"cello caruso-turiello\", \"original_dimensions\": {\"width\": 2048, \"height\": 1364}}, \"photos_locked\": false, \"wikipedia_url\": null, \"iconic_taxon_id\": 3, \"iconic_taxon_name\": \"Aves\", \"listed_taxa_count\": 92, \"wikipedia_summary\": \"El <b>suirirí piquirrojo</b> (<i><b>Dendrocygna autummalis</b></i>), también conocido como <b>suirirí piquirrojo</b> (Perú), <b>güíchichi</b> (Panamá), <b>pisingo</b>, <b>pichichi</b>, <b>pichihuila</b> (en Sinaloa), <b>pijije</b> (en el sur de México) o <b>pisingo</b> (en Colombia) es una especie de ave anseriforme de la familia Anatidae ampliamente difundida en América.\", \"observations_count\": 48025, \"conservation_status\": null, \"english_common_name\": \"Pisingo\", \"establishment_means\": {\"id\": 211972, \"place\": {\"id\": 7196, \"name\": \"Colombia\", \"ancestry\": \"97389\", \"display_name\": \"Colombia\"}, \"establishment_means\": \"native\"}, \"taxon_changes_count\": 0, \"taxon_schemes_count\": 9, \"conservation_statuses\": [{\"id\": 2406, \"url\": \"https://www.iucnredlist.org/species/22679780/131907111\", \"iucn\": 10, \"place\": null, \"status\": \"LC\", \"updater\": {\"id\": 2059107, \"login\": \"victor_85\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"taxon_id\": 6893, \"authority\": \"IUCN Red List\", \"source_id\": 18766, \"created_at\": \"2013-02-16T00:51:19+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": null, \"taxon_name\": \"Dendrocygna autumnalis\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2022-03-25T09:57:18+00:00\", \"updater_id\": 2059107, \"description\": \"\"}, {\"id\": 262837, \"url\": \"https://uicn.fr/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/tableaux-liste-rouge-faune-vertebree-de-guyane.pdf\", \"iucn\": 50, \"user\": {\"id\": 2059107, \"login\": \"victor_85\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"place\": {\"id\": 6949, \"name\": \"French Guiana\", \"admin_level\": 0, \"display_name\": \"French Guiana\", \"ancestor_place_ids\": [97389, 6949]}, \"status\": \"CR\", \"updater\": {\"id\": 2059107, \"login\": \"victor_85\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"taxon_id\": 6893, \"authority\": \"UICN Comité Français\", \"source_id\": null, \"created_at\": \"2022-03-25T09:57:18+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": \"open\", \"taxon_name\": \"Dendrocygna autumnalis\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2025-04-05T14:31:45+00:00\", \"updater_id\": 2059107, \"description\": \"Le Dendrocygne à ventre noir présente une population nicheuse de taille restreinte, en déclin et estimée à moins de 250 individus, tous regroupés en une seule population. Sa tendance actuelle est à la diminution. Si la population guyanaise est fortement connectée à celle du Suriname, qui rencontre les mêmes menaces et avec des échanges réguliers, ces derniers ne consituent pas d\'apports significatifs pouvant réduire le risque de disparition de l\'espèce en Guyane.\"}, {\"id\": 160302, \"url\": \"https://biblioteca.ambiente.gob.ar/wp-content/uploads/Categorizacion-de-aves-de-la-Argentina.pdf\", \"iucn\": 10, \"user\": {\"id\": 1368063, \"login\": \"goncrisdi\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"place\": {\"id\": 7190, \"name\": \"Argentina\", \"admin_level\": 0, \"display_name\": \"Argentina\", \"ancestor_place_ids\": [97389, 7190]}, \"status\": \"NA\", \"updater\": {\"id\": 2059107, \"login\": \"victor_85\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"taxon_id\": 6893, \"authority\": \"Ministerio de Ambiente y Desarrollo Sustentable y Aves Argentina - 2017\", \"source_id\": null, \"created_at\": \"2020-08-02T16:04:32+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": \"open\", \"taxon_name\": \"Dendrocygna autumnalis\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2025-04-05T14:31:37+00:00\", \"updater_id\": 2059107, \"description\": \"\"}], \"preferred_common_name\": \"Pisingo\", \"complete_species_count\": null, \"current_synonymous_taxon_ids\": null, \"preferred_establishment_means\": \"native\"}], \"per_page\": 30, \"total_results\": 1}', NULL, '2025-12-16 05:53:59', '2025-12-15 20:02:36', 1, '2025-12-15 05:53:59', '2025-12-15 20:02:36');
