7, originalmente bajo el nombre <i>Aranea clavipes</i>.​​ El nombre del género <i>Trichonephila</i> se deriva de las palabras griegas \\\"nen\\\" que significa hilar y \\\"philos\\\", que significa amor, amistad, afecto, por lo que se le da el significado de \\\"aficionada a hilar\\\". El nombre de la especie proviene de las palabras latinas...\", \"observations_count\": 57429, \"conservation_status\": null, \"english_common_name\": \"Golden Silk Spider\", \"establishment_means\": {\"id\": 7840421, \"place\": {\"id\": 7196, \"name\": \"Colombia\", \"ancestry\": \"97389\", \"display_name\": \"Colombia\"}, \"establishment_means\": \"native\"}, \"taxon_changes_count\": 1, \"taxon_schemes_count\": 0, \"conservation_statuses\": [{\"id\": 220660, \"url\": \"https://www.iucnredlist.org/species/89292313/89292873\", \"iucn\": 10, \"place\": null, \"status\": \"LC\", \"taxon_id\": 904336, \"authority\": \"IUCN Red List\", \"source_id\": null, \"created_at\": \"2021-09-29T05:19:52+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": \"open\", \"taxon_name\": \"Trichonephila clavipes\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2021-09-29T05:19:52+00:00\", \"updater_id\": null, \"description\": null}], \"preferred_common_name\": \"Araña de seda dorada\", \"complete_species_count\": null, \"current_synonymous_taxon_ids\": null, \"preferred_establishment_means\": \"native\"}], \"per_page\": 30, \"total_results\": 1}', NULL, '2025-12-17 06:46:40', '2025-12-16 06:46:40', 0, '2025-12-15 05:55:27', '2025-12-16 06:46:40'),
