ución comprende desde Panamá hasta el norte de Paraguay y Bolivia, pasando por toda la cuenca amazónica. En cautividad se reproducen fácilmente; en libertad viven en grupos de 25-30 ejemplares. Este loro es el representante inconfundible de los...\", \"observations_count\": 10817, \"conservation_status\": {\"id\": 139961, \"url\": \"http://www.cites.org/eng/resources/species.html\", \"iucn\": 40, \"user\": {\"id\": 477, \"login\": \"loarie\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"place\": {\"id\": 97389, \"name\": \"South America\", \"admin_level\": -10, \"display_name\": \"South America\", \"ancestor_place_ids\": [97389]}, \"status\": \"Appendix II\", \"updater\": {\"id\": 477, \"login\": \"loarie\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"taxon_id\": 19018, \"authority\": \"CITES\", \"source_id\": null, \"created_at\": \"2018-03-16T03:39:34+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": \"obscured\", \"taxon_name\": \"Ara ararauna\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2020-05-24T23:55:32+00:00\", \"updater_id\": 477, \"description\": \"\"}, \"english_common_name\": \"Blue-and-yellow Macaw\", \"establishment_means\": {\"id\": 159015, \"place\": {\"id\": 7196, \"name\": \"Colombia\", \"ancestry\": \"97389\", \"display_name\": \"Colombia\"}, \"establishment_means\": \"native\"}, \"taxon_changes_count\": 0, \"taxon_schemes_count\": 7, \"conservation_statuses\": [{\"id\": 7769, \"url\": \"https://www.iucnredlist.org/species/22685539/131917270\", \"iucn\": 10, \"place\": null, \"status\": \"LC\", \"updater\": {\"id\": 2059107, \"login\": \"victor_85\", \"orcid\": null, \"icon_url\": null}, \"taxon_id\": 19018, \"authority\": \"IUCN Red List\", \"source_id\": 18766, \"created_at\": \"2013-02-16T00:54:08+00:00\", \"geoprivacy\": null, \"taxon_name\": \"Ara ararauna\", \"taxon_rank\": \"species\", \"updated_at\": \"2022-03-25T13:26:00+00:00\", \"updater_id\": 2059107, \"description\": \"\"}, {\"id\": 139961, \"url\": \"http://www.cites.org/eng/resources/species.html\", \"iucn\": 4